        "modelingNotes": [
          "The orderNumber field lists an electronic module plus its required connection module. This is a documented two-part assembly, not a single Siemens order number.",
          "Every exposed field-connector pin is inventoried, including unassigned pins. Terminal keys Xn.p identify connector Xn, physical pin p. Descriptive signal names are not alternative physical terminals.",
          "The internal backplane contacts, module-to-module power distribution, protective behavior and configuration are not modeled. No backplane supply screw terminals are invented.",
          "Connector pin metadata, functions and repeated 1M/2M/FE/Us labels do not join physical nets. Author any verified conductor continuity explicitly. No-connection positions are inventory annotations; a do-not-wire rule is not implemented.",
          "Connector presence is separate from electrical continuity. A cable assembly with an unresolved pin map does not satisfy a required electrical terminal. Unused socket sealing and hardware installation requirements remain project review items.",
          "Voltage output ranges are ±10 V, 0–10 V and 1–5 V. QV+ and QV- remain separate endpoints; neither output reference is automatically tied to the connector 1M supply return."
        ]
